  "reply": "I rewrote `parseDuration` in `src/duration.ts`, and `bun test` passes (26 tests, 0 failures). I changed no other file.\n\n- **Accepted input:** one or more nonnegative integer components in strict `h`, `m`, `s`, `ms` order, with optional whitespace between components and at both ends. It returns the total in milliseconds.\n- **Rejected input:** empty or whitespace-only input, duplicate or out-of-order units, signs, fractions and junk all throw `RangeError`. So does any total above `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`.\n- **Large values:** the sum uses `BigInt`, so a huge digit string can't lose precision before the size check.\n- **Unchanged:** the `parseDuration` export and its signature, and the library stays dependency-free per `CLAUDE.md`.\n\nI read the existing tests only through the `bun test` result.",
